Chapter: TcoFramedAppendTest

 A self-tail-recursive loop whose only subroutine call is hidden inside
 a binary operator: the text append in the tail argument lowers to a
 call to `__str_concat`. The `when` refuses the frameless path, so the
 loop is framed, and a frame emitter that believes the body makes no
 call saves no `ra` and returns into itself, which reads as a hang
 rather than a fault.

Section: Types

  Step =
   | Go
   | Stop

Section: Helpers

  step-of : Integer -> Step
  step-of (n) = if n <= 0 then Stop else Go

  by-append-text : Integer, Text -> Text
  by-append-text (n) (acc) =
    when step-of n
     is Stop -> acc
     is Go -> by-append-text (n - 1) (acc & "x")

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni "01 start"
    print-line-uni ("02 append-text " & show (text-length (by-append-text 4 "")))
    print-line-uni "03 done"
  end
